      {"id": "journal-001", "date": "2026-09-24", "title": "Reflective Monday — Planning the week ahead", "content": "Today I reflected on my financial situation. The CIBIL report shows a score of 741, which is decent but there's room for improvement. The ICICI #1 card balance is concerning — at 74% utilization, it's dragging down my score. Need to focus on paying that down.\n\nAlso reviewed my career goals. The Tech Lead goal is still 2 years away. Need to make sure I'm building the right skills and taking on the right responsibilities.\n\nOn the fitness front, feeling good. Running consistently, meditation practice is building. Need to keep the momentum.", "mood": "Reflective", "tags": ["reflection", "finance", "career", "fitness"], "privacy": "private", "created_at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00Z"},
      {"id": "journal-002", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Maharashtra Trip — Looking back", "content": "The Maharashtra monsoon ride was incredible. From Pune to Malshej Ghat — the scenery was breathtaking. Met some amazing people along the way.\n\nKey takeaways:\n- Planning is everything for a trip this size\n- Toothless performed flawlessly over 1200 km\n- Need to build more content from this trip for YouTube\n- The monsoon adds a whole new dimension to riding", "mood": "Grateful", "tags": ["travel", "maharashtra", "reflection", "bike"], "privacy": "private", "created_at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00Z"}
